<title>UK: William Cook shares gain after 400.7p bid.</title>
<headline>William Cook shares gain after 400.7p bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in steel products group William Cook Plc advanced in pre-market trade on Monday after engineering group Triplex Lloyd raised its bid for the company.</p>
<p>The shares were indicated 15p higher at 390p.</p>
<p>Triplex said its increased offer of 400.7 pence per share was final. The revised offer values the group at around 74.8 million stg.</p>
<p>Triplex launched its initial hostile bid in November which was worth around 309 pence per share, valuing William Cook at just under 58 million stg.  Shares in William Cook stood at 240p the day before the initial bid.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
